    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0603" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3924</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-19T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your cipher telegram of April 17, midnight. The Chinese Minister has been aware
                    for some time of possibilities of the situation.</p>
                <p>My telegram of April 14, 4 p.m., is not to be taken as limiting assistance to
                    amount mentioned in your telegram of February 6, 11 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d629-f1"/> Reference to that and one other telegram was to indicate
                    that offer is in response to Chinese request. The bill authorizing financial
                    assistance to powers at war with our enemies passed House and Senate
                    unanimously, but owing to some difference in provisions has been sent to
                    conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
